       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg per dose three times daily comes to 15 g/day, which is almost four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for adults. A single 5 g dose is already above the normal single-dose limit of 1 g, and 15 g/day carries a serious risk of acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual ceiling)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the 5,000 mg dose for a specific reason, tell me the clinical context. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy before it goes into the system."
