       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 15 g/day it would very likely cause severe liver injury or death, and no clinical context I can think of supports it. I don't want to put an order into the system that I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right now.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily, or four times daily at most. I can add a note such as \"max 4 g/day from all sources.\"\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to get more analgesia or antipyresis, I can enter a multimodal regimen. That could include an NSAID if appropriate, or other agents you choose.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you think there's a reason for an exception, such as a typo in the source order or a protocol I don't know about, the pharmacy or the medical director can review it and override it through the proper channel.\n\nTell me which of these you want and I'll enter it."
      }
